# JMarkdown mode demo :label[demo-top]

Every construct the highlighter knows, in one file. Open it, then try
`C-c` commands, the JMarkdown menu, folding on the blocks below, and
`C-c C-p` for the math preview.

## Inline formatting

This paragraph has *bold text*, /italic text/, **intense text**,
__underlined text__, ==highlighted text==, `inline code`, and a
[link](https://example.com). Escaped slashes work /inside \/an\/ italic
span/, while paths like /usr/bin and fractions like 1/2 stay plain.
Times like 3:30 and ratios a:b are not directives, but :today is, and
so is :ref[demo-top].

Mustache variables: dear {{name}}, your total is {{total}}.

## Math

Inline math $e^{i\pi} + 1 = 0$ and display math:

$$
\int_0^\infty e^{-x^2}\,dx = \frac{\sqrt{\pi}}{2}
$$

Bracket form \(a^2 + b^2 = c^2\) and an environment:

\begin{align}
  \nabla \cdot \mathbf{E} &= \frac{\rho}{\varepsilon_0} \\
  \nabla \cdot \mathbf{B} &= 0
\end{align}

## Citations and footnotes

As argued in \citep[see][p. 42]{alexander2024}, structure emerges from
dynamics.[^why: This is the labelled footnote body, attached at the
call site.] Sometimes anonymously.[fn: An anonymous footnote.]

## Directives

:::note[A titled note]{.fancy #note-1 author="me"}
Directive bodies are ordinary markdown: *bold*, /italic/, $x^2$.
:::

::::aside
Containers nest by colon count.

:::warning
Three colons inside four.
:::
::::

Inline format-specific output: :TeX[\noindent] is LaTeX-only, while
:HTML[<em>web-only</em>] is HTML-only.

## Environments

@begin(theorem)[Euclid]{.numbered}
There are infinitely many primes. The body is markdown: /italic/,
*bold*, math $p_1 p_2 \cdots p_n + 1$.
@end(theorem)

@begin(equation*)
\hat{H}\psi = E\psi
@end(equation*)

## Diagrams

:::TiKZ
\begin{tikzpicture}
  \draw[->] (0,0) -- (2,1) node[right] {$x$};
  \node at (1, -0.3) {a vector};
\end{tikzpicture}
:::

:::mermaid
graph TD
  A[Start] -->|yes| B{Decision}
  B --> C((Done))
  subgraph The Loop
    C --> A
  end
  classDef green fill:#9f6,stroke:#333
  class C green
%% a comment
:::

@begin(mermaid)
sequenceDiagram
  participant A as Alice
  A->>B: Hello
  Note over A,B: greeting
@end(mermaid)

## Embedded JavaScript

The answer is compute(6, 7).label and pluralize.word("editor") in
prose. Script blocks pass through:

<script data-type="jmarkdown">
let total = 6 * 7;
global.output = `Total: ${total}`;
</script>

## Code fences

```js
// A fenced block highlights in its own language.
const x = [1, 2, 3].map((n) => n * 2);
```

```lisp
(define (greet) (insert! "hello"))
```

## Inclusion

[[chapter-2.jmd]]

That is the lot. Fold the sections from the gutter, and the directive
and environment blocks from their opening lines.
